[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718873227","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6718873227","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6718873227,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHneiw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:43:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:43:24Z","body":"Two additional source-partonomy findings are confirmed within this preparation-family issue: `W05-FINAL-CHEM-NEW-02` and `W05-FINAL-CHEM-NEW-03`. Their original before-fix reports and all four published payload hashes are preserved; this is a proposed correction, not acceptance of the full successor.\n\n| Existing proposal | Primary evidence and supported whole-stock description |\n|---|---|\n| CHEM-C1193-HEPES-1221 and CHEM-C1193-HEPES-1474 | [NBRC1221](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1221) and [NBRC1474](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1474) specify a 1 M HEPES-KOH additive. The separately stated receiving-medium pH values do not specify stock pH. |\n| CHEM-C1193-DSMZ_394_1137-Tris | [DSMZ394](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium394.pdf) and [DSMZ1137](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1137.pdf) specify a 1 M Tris-HCl stock at pH7.5, with different receiving doses. |\n| CHEM-C1193-JCM_1061-Tris | [JCM1061](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1061) specifies a 0.5 M Tris-HCl stock at pH8.0. |\n\nAll five primary documents were fetched successfully for this check. None enumerates the proposed stock's preparation inputs. The candidates nevertheless use `RECIPE_TRANSCRIPTION` to assert total buffer moieties and potassium-containing or chloride species as material components. Those descriptions are inferred chemical/speciation categories. Under MAPPING_SEMANTICS section6, an ion or speciation bridge cannot stand in for a material has-part assertion. Nominal stock strength does not establish free-base/salt fractions, potassium stoichiometry or separately supplied free KOH/HCl. Merely changing the assertion method would not make these material inputs supported.\n\nThe bounded correction is to omit the unsupported `components` and their paired `component_assertion`, while retaining the useful whole-stock names, source-stated strengths/pH, exact occurrence routing, evidence, original history and explicit unknown composition. Do not substitute dry Tris hydrochloride, infer solvent or titration inputs, borrow receiving-medium water/pH, or treat unknown stock details as proof that the two HEPES preparations differ. This does not change the separate solid Tris-HCl parent-grade finding in #1238. Full successor review and native validation remain required; no owner, role or export approval follows.\n\nReproduction is saved at `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/buffer-source-parts-triage-v1/`. Original finding SHA256s: `ef1bc8a7f7ea8ff459305fb71b1864baec2d3c8fff72df3855d79b428aea0f49` and `99be33af59ae5ea2abad4f7df98b414b528147047076357bc5b21b48043412f9`. Payload hashes are `05cf4a1b09aff0fd1954ef0ac1aa563844414f4896261eaca48271323d9f8a46`, `6ba28f7de8b9b6387fb38f44ec01ce9b9626a84bea256ea63b7d0df07b109fad`, `0f8cf263079c547959a4b82831900988b2e07df24eb59c51e62e97fb675733ac`, and `9009b7dc6651004a025591c4e9376e117d4978bc7049b91e2001352bcf83561b`.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718873227/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718921474","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6718921474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6718921474,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHqbAg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:48:58Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:48:58Z","body":"Reviewed W02 head `0597d00417be4d7cdfb5a31970043eec9bbc88fe`, frozen campaign base `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`. Authoritative peer review is `assembly-v2/review.yaml` (SHA256 `31cac38cae0cfb3dcfae4453a01402dc98d249f70ad9a7698a89b25eed5eae11`) in the sealed W04 independent W02 packet, whose 2,399-member SHA256SUMS is `99306617655b1e3df84368079e49f4341a0fd05667bdf9fedf18dda24f4f7ca7`. The coordinator verified all manifest members, rebound all188 case decisions and106 selected payloads, and independently repeated all106 native guarded writes and baseline/overlay partonomy. Structural validation passes; the scientific verdict remains needs_curation. These are unapplied proposal corrections, not changes already made to main or whole-owner/export approval.\n\nAdd the exact W02 preparation-family extension `W02-F-IRON-STOCK-DUPLICATE` (`w02-external-b-004`), cases53/176. The [DSMZ718 recipe](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium718.pdf) (SHA256 `09faeca86ec0358bcdc3b5674e2323ac61c3ca554a9323bb09eb6f06fa6feb1c`) and [DSMZ399 recipe](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium399.pdf) (`29f9f4df24231ba04f8113f3f7b6d8fd82b186c000608627ad02905808ae7ed0`) both state the literal seven-water ferrous ammonium sulfate stock at0.1%w/v,2mL receiving dose. One candidate expresses1g/L, which is the same stated strength.\n\n| Proposal | Owner | Exact selected SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a2-proposal-dsmz718-ferrous-ammonium-sulfate-stock` | `data/ingredients/mapped/dsmz718_ferrous_ammonium_sulfate_stock.yaml` | `4c8c6b0ee75793b83bddc54f795c249084429aa86e306abd44212c3316d9f818` |\n| `c2-proposal-ferrous-ammonium-heptahydrate-stock` | `data/ingredients/mapped/dsmz399_ferrous_ammonium_sulfate_heptahydrate_0_1pct_wv_stock.yaml` | `afcdaa60b415472c2a2663da9f52475149aeb080248cce0598f606d86c837f2b` |\n\nReconcile the overlapping supported partial-preparation scope into one justified nominal candidate or establish a positive material distinction before co-installation. Do not infer complete formulation equivalence from the same listed solute/strength; unknown solvent/batch details are neither proof of equality nor disjointness. Preserve both exact source/case lineages and the literal seven waters without silently converting to conventional Mohr hexahydrate. The sealed review's stronger early phrase \"same stock\" is qualified by its final root adjudication, which does not assert full composition equivalence.\n\nThe separate W02-F-PREPARATIONS DSMZ375/1107 cysteine overlap is a second family dependency under1201. Keep375's unknown strength/solvent/filtration distinct from1107's explicit5%w/v scope; do not create a chemically disjoint owner solely because source numbers differ. These exact families were not present in the previously sealed1237 family packet (ignored-inclusive comparison); this comment adds scope without duplicating its common identity rule.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6718921474/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719045392","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6719045392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6719045392,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHx_EA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:03:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:03:22Z","body":"Independent successor readback at `ee75d464c4a44edfbc57c72c200eeeaf962a7192` confirms the already disclosed `W07-SKEPTIC-LEDGER-PARTIAL-001` (native key `MediaIngredientMech.W07.JCM900-historical-PARTIAL-draft-pointer`). This is one minor inherited ledger inconsistency, not an additional chemical-identity finding.\n\nThe two case IDs below still use “separately proposed JCM900 nominal stock with PARTIAL assertion” in active reasoning/applicability, although both select `W07-COMBINED-JCM900-JCM979-Hutner`, whose complete immediate source list is `COMPLETE`. The new integration note already says the old wording is historical and must not override that selection.\n\n- `CM_NAME:413f665d954f387d2bf0a3baa2ce2bdfdd043dcc43532d442db0b16ca85a2fe2`\n- `CM_NAME:506bbe669107e7f2e69edfd707da8af99be9ec015f6e68c77ee9e9cf9532a5a3`\n\nBefore final integration, make a separate immutable ledger-only correction: point active text to the combined selected proposal and distinguish COMPLETE printed input-list closure from unresolved molybdate/nested chemical identity. Preserve historical text and all source cases/occurrences and payloads; do not change stock identity, amounts, role or release status. The reviewer reproduced this using the exact published decisions and payload; no new whole-owner approval is conveyed. Root should use the existing1237 scope or another exact existing lineage issue after dedup rather than duplicate this already identified lead.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719045392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719045619","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6719045619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6719045619,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkHx_8w","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:03:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:03:24Z","body":"Four-family independent review follow-up: two minor Columbia evidence-packet findings, with the ownership block retained.\n\nThe completed W06 review covers the exact DAIGO188/474, phosphate873/940, Hutner624/657 and Columbia300/921 candidates: eight origins, twelve source cases and fifteen CultureMech occurrences. Its three independent reviewer scopes and native saved review were checked. The 315-member review packet and 347-member author packet rehash. Ten-vitamin573/810 is excluded from scientific acceptance because W06 authored an origin.\n\n- **W06-FF-001 / FFA-001 — frozen M2224 recipe binding.** The author packet references the full `columbia_blood_agar_oxoid.yaml` recipe but does not carry its bytes. The original frozen queue copy and independently recovered copy both hash to `2db87e5a52686a3592ac32eafdd18b2a9ddb64f849469d73f06f9483ad23e0a8`. Bind that exact complete recipe and its source-case/occurrence in a new immutable handoff, preserving the old packet. No formula change is required.\n- **W06-FF-002 / FFA-002 — qualify the current Difco 44 g contrast.** The exact original W10 capture `9d330adf2da453b5e03f506b7f37fcca3f39dfb0f36cee6b6357914cefaaa1fb` contains a substantive indexed extraction from the official BD manual: the seven-part Difco Columbia table and 44 g instruction, separately from the BBL table. It is not merely a title, and no contradiction of 44 g was established. The author packet carries the evidence-ledger reference but not this capture. The direct PDF request failed, so a complete PDF/page-image verification must not be claimed. Either bind the exact indexed capture and state those retrieval limits, or remove the unnecessary numeric contrast from current notes. Preserve the inherited history verbatim. This does not create a universal full-PDF gate.\n\nDAIGO's nominal product scope, the two equal-volume 1 M phosphate inputs, and the nominal Hutner family remain supported within their existing limits. Preserve the 3.15 g versus 3.2 g DAIGO distinction, unknown phosphate carrier/hydration/pH, the Hutner 3.335 g versus 3.34 g precision, malformed molybdate literals, nested stock/process unknowns and all genuine source holds. An existing Metals44 alias match does not itself authorize a chemically complete nested-stock reference.\n\n**Columbia remains `BLOCKED_OWNER_CONTINUITY`.** Support for the nominal Oxoid 39 g formulation does not partition the authentic mixed `UNMAPPED_0118` owner, assign a historical catalog code to M2224, establish a prepared blood-agar product, or approve a role or export. Preserve the genuine Oxoid/Difco source histories until an explicit owner-boundary decision and all required couplings are reviewed.\n\nAll eight currently published origins were rebound to their exact cases and payloads. Six payloads are unchanged. W07 origins624/657 at `ee75d464c4a44edfbc57c72c200eeeaf962a7192` have only the approved mapping-evidence type correction and appended history; their selector expressly forbids separate co-installation. Carry that current provenance through the shared candidate successor without choosing an individual winner. This mechanical bridge is not a substitute for the separate W07 successor review or final integrated application review.\n\nEvidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/four-family-review-triage-v1/{HANDOFF.json,disposition-matrix.json,current-origin-bridges.json,FF002-independent-qualification.json}`. Original W06 native review SHA256 `fb76dd2554d57e225fbdca8bce51091be81c2b640bc4c2f35fdd8b0dc8db2830`; its first category/key validation failure and the native metadata-only correction are retained. No candidate, maintained record, gate or review history was edited by this triage.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719045619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719103915","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6719103915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6719103915,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkH1jqw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:09:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:09:55Z","body":"Independent follow-up `W10-SV3-SKEPTIC-CALF-BLOOD-WORDING` is confirmed against published W10 head `c9a96da71a1977014680e5a92e600dfc7e3874db`. This is a minor explanation error in proposal `sv1-bio-calf_blood_togo_m2854`, case 44; the source-supported blood identity and broader blood mapping remain intact.\n\nThe active notes, mapping-evidence explanation and proposal description say “Calf age class distinguishes it from serum.” Age and material fraction are separate attributes: calf serum also exists. The exact [TOGO M2854 recipe](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2854) names **calf blood** at a literal 10% receiving dose. It does not explicitly say “whole,” specify a percentage basis, or establish defibrination, lysis or a commercial product. The root readback verified the committed source capture `12f6464a1dcc66a32160e85433034cfd067ea5e930f3ae6d12ce2c60d6af2770` and selected payload `62f0dc3300c488be2fb9d52f2c65e8e6826715d81177cf8e4ce48af422ed7338`.\n\nBounded correction: state that the source names calf blood, a blood material rather than serum, while calf specifies developmental origin. Correct current explanatory fields and any exact active case/proposal reasoning that repeats the error. Preserve the original historical event verbatim and append a truthful correction event. Keep the source label, identifier, mapping, unknown processing, unknown percentage basis, source-specific applicability, nonresolving generic label and all role/export holds unchanged. Do not infer a new product or expand aliases.\n\nThis was disclosed by a separate skeptical reviewer before any fix; the provenance-only correction did not endorse the inherited wording. Make an immutable successor with exact changed-field accounting, native checks and independent review. Current issue search found no separate calf-blood wording tracker, so this follow-up stays on the existing family issue. Private evidence and the original finding are retained under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w10-calf-wording-triage-v1/`.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719103915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719236644","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6719236644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6719236644,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkH9qJA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:24:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:24:38Z","body":"Independent ten-vitamin reconciliation found four concrete source/owner conditions, tracked here before any correction (TV-001 through TV-004).\n\n1. **TV-001 — ATCC owner protocol/product scope.** The maintained `ATCC_Wolfes_Vitamin_Mix` component list cites the ten-vitamin ATCC2672 protocol without phosphate, while its history identifies MD-VS. The current official [MD-VS formulation](https://www.atcc.org/products/md-vs) includes monopotassium phosphate at 900 mg/L. Both inspected upstream CultureBotHT exact ATCC-name definitions identify MD-VS and contain phosphate. Preserve these distinct source claims and original history; source-definition linkage does not prove a purchased lot or historical lot composition.\n2. **TV-002 — listed water is not exact final volume.** The protocol tables list batch solute masses and 1 L distilled water input. They do not establish a make-to-volume instruction. The maintained protocol-derived MG_PER_L and L_PER_L values need correction or an explicit independently evidenced basis. MD-VS's directly printed mg/L values are a different source claim. Do not infer displacement, density or a final-volume denominator.\n3. **TV-003 — existing generic owner continuity.** `Wolfes_Vitamin_Mix` originates in CultureBotHT, then acquires a phosphate-containing NCMA component assertion. The inspected upstream generic definitions contain ten vitamins, no phosphate, and explicit cyanocobalamin. Reconcile the authentic original/current source lineage before reusing this owner or minting a new nominal ten-vitamin owner. This does not prove the NCMA formula is wrong, and generic B12 must not silently become cyanocobalamin in the JCM/NBRC recipe.\n4. **TV-004 — nonuniform ATCC X1 scale.** The upstream exact ATCC definition labels X=1. Its ten vitamin values are one hundredth of the current MD-VS concentrations after unit comparison, while phosphate 0.9 g/L equals MD-VS 900 mg/L. A single dilution factor cannot reconcile the whole block. Preserve raw quantities, forms and X metadata and establish stock versus receiving-medium scope; do not silently repair the source.\n\nThe independently supported immediate result is one source-qualified nominal JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 recipe representation, preserving all ten literal vitamins, 1 L water input and each preparation method. There is a positive boundary from the MD-VS product/source-definition scope; a missing D stereochemical qualifier is not evidence of a distinct substance. Creating a fresh owner remains blocked on the genuine generic-owner continuity decision. Perfect molecular specification is not a prerequisite for documenting the nominal recipe.\n\nThe review accounts for eight cases and 71 CultureMech occurrences, with six excluded contexts and 84 separate KG holds. Its 65-context upper bound is not blanket mapping approval. Current W06 `1d62a4084cda998064110c0e6ddfbf943b52c3de` and W08 `1701ccf2049022866adfcebcc9bba9b6492407c6` origins are explicitly bridged. The new W08 component bindings and exact alias need their own field-level review; no role, whole-owner or export approval is conferred.\n\nEvidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/w07/worktree/.temp/ten-vitamin-owner-boundary-independent-v1/`, active `HANDOFF-v2.json` SHA256 `5c57ac577453d1a7dc19444b7d50bff5c37d9b6367915114d673034421871c77`, manifest `a8082a5bd23dbad4cf5eaacea475a1ec6474c79169edea68fdb37737be7d2cfd` (683 members rehashed by coordinator), scientific adjudication `e9badf652fced9acc15e01a9f1ccd7a575360cf11d568b50aee760ac07a5ed01`. Exact primary captures, original owner beforeimages, source routes and three independent reviewer scopes are retained. No maintained correction has been applied.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719236644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719499726","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6719499726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6719499726,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkINtzg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:53:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:53:52Z","body":"Independent follow-up on TV-003 and the nominal ten-vitamin scope confirms a supported correction on the authentic existing `data/ingredients/mapped/Wolfes_Vitamin_Mix.yaml` owner. Its CultureBotHT import/classification/registry promotion precedes the later NCMA component annotation. The current raw `Mixes.csv` generic block names ten solutes at its printed mg/L values, including cyanocobalamin; X100 is retained as separate metadata, with no multiplication or division. The preserved April count61 and its58 unrecovered member identities do not block this current source correction. Do not replace that historical statistic with the later62/63 counts.\n\nExact private candidate `fe6070272f269fde7683696e4c46a331902ab88baac8c5cc93db7bddf9d0ec1b` changes only components, component assertion, notes and one appended history event; all original history, identity, aliases, roles and other fields remain. Ten literal source components deliberately remain ungrounded in this bounded candidate. This is not a conclusion that suitable child IDs do not exist; final composition must incorporate the separate exact child-identity reviews without approval transfer.\n\nAdditional exact target `CONT-NCMA-WATER-001` belongs here under TV-002/TV-003: before-owner SHA256 `709749bd7c83c38a09400fc1893885ead753847ff9d1cbbe4ec76b431d349738` gives `components[11]` distilled water1.0L_PER_L. The complete [official NCMA6 source](https://ncma.bigelow.org/PDF%20Files/NCMA%20Medium%206%20Wolfe%27s%20Vitamin%20Solution.pdf), PDF SHA256 `b7bbf28efb43cfee8476e83780a55d929e574f3f0b7479583926d927409b4615`, specifies eleven solutes per litre and water/filter preparation, but no numeric water quantity. Preserve the genuine NCMA phosphate-containing source claim. A separately retained NCMA assertion must keep water unquantified; the CB candidate already replaces the unbridged NCMA decomposition under TV-003. No separate NCMA owner is silently created or repaired.\n\n[JCM197](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197), [NBRC837](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=837) and [NBRC903](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=903) support the nominal ten-vitamin batch recipe now, including the listed water input and source-specific preparation. Perfect molecular/lot specification is not needed to document it. The remaining decision concerns only exact association with the more specific CB cyanocobalamin/concentration/X100 scope; generic B12 and a listed water input must not inherit that specificity. Section3 permits a reviewed explicit nominal convention with details retained; it does not justify duplicate source-number owners or infer equality/difference from missing details. Treat this as a bounded representation/applicability obligation, not a new human-only permission gate.\n\nAll eight cases,71CM occurrences,84KG holds and six exclusions remain accounted. The65-context upper bound is not blanket mapping approval; exact aliases, child bindings, roles and exports remain separate. TV-001/TV-002/TV-004 are not closed. Independent checks rehashed980packet members, reproduced3closed-schema validations and baseline/overlay partonomy2956, checked actual historical Git blobs and all71recipe pointers. Evidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/tenvit-continuity-triage-v1/assessment.json`; original W09 packet and reviewer identities are unchanged. No maintained application occurred.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6719499726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720042215","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720042215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720042215,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkIu05w","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:53:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:53:21Z","body":"The current independent nominal-recipe review supports consolidating the JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 source proposals into one report-level ten-vitamin recipe. It identifies an additional authentic maintained comparator, `Mc_vitamins`, whose CultureBotHT Mixes block has the same ten numeric amounts after g-to-mg conversion. Existing-owner reuse versus a distinct material scope needs this concrete continuity assessment before installation. Missing D/DL specificity or added-water versus per-litre wording establishes neither identity nor difference. No second source-number owner is approved; all source and export holds remain.\n\nA confirmed existing component-reference defect is recorded here before correction as **SCI-TENVIT-003**: `data/ingredients/mapped/Mc_vitamins.yaml` components[6] names **calcium D,L-pantothenate**, consistent with primary CultureBotHT Mixes.csv row1122, but uses `CHEBI:31345`. The [primary ChEBI record](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:31345) has a stereospecific structure, D-calcium pantothenate synonyms and CAS137-08-6. That reference does not establish the explicitly D,L component. Preserve the literal source and exact quantity; select a child only with same-form evidence, otherwise withdraw the unsupported resolving reference. The new nominal JCM/NBRC candidates already keep calcium stereochemistry unresolved. This finding does not establish whole-stock identity, authorize a merge, or change role approval.\n\nThe root checked current GitHub search results for Mc_vitamins and pantothenate and the existing TV001–004 comments; this is an addition to the same bounded family issue, not a duplicate issue. The earlier NCMA-versus-CB attribution obligation and lipoic-acid catalog qualification remain explicitly inherited, rather than new blanket blockers.\n\nEvidence: `workers/w04/worktree/.temp/tenvit-nominal-reconciliation-independent-v1/` under the campaign root. Handoff SHA256 `40de7f6c1eca6d9084f510a534cf9b49b9fa03dea1806079b070289b9f81f515`; manifest `c963f7255725afedeaaf09037209591f6633efa4740e7afda9e9e60b0b689b7f` (all179 members rehashed by coordinator); final selector `dcdef5a08730540873425e3167d2495b2e50b76089c2772a5c4677852c25d870`. Actual primary/scientific, skeptical and final-assembly reviewer identities and scopes are retained. No maintained correction or release has been applied.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720042215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720120537","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720120537","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720120537,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkIzm2Q","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:02:10Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:02:10Z","body":"The three remaining CENTRAL-31 comparisons have author-independent support for bounded common scopes, before any maintained application:\n\n- **NTA stocks:** [NBRC1020](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1020), [NBRC824](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=824) and [JCM284](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=284) agree on ten named dry inputs and masses, plus water/KOH and the initial 200 mL/pH6.5 step. Use one nominal recipe, preserving both source preparation profiles. JCM alone establishes final1L and pH7. Common quantities are batch masses; water/KOH remain globally unquantified. Do not assert NBRC final pH or volume, 1.2L water, common final concentration or dissolved speciation.\n- **Seven-acid VFA:** the [3774 table](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/solution/3774) and [608 table](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/solution/608) support one explicitly nominal recipe with both exact ordered input vectors: 17/6/4/1/1/1/1mL and 548.5/193.5/129/32.25/32.25/32.25/32.25mL. Six entries scale32.25; acetate differs by0.25mL. This is not exact numerical equality or a primary assertion of rounding. Keep both profiles, omit unqualified common numeric component amounts, and introduce no average, tolerance or additive final volume.\n- **Water:** the inspected DSMZ recipe contexts and primary ELGA laboratory guide page5 support the ordinary shared deionized/demineralized, unspecified ion-removal-grade sense. Retain the local grade identity and molecular-water parent boundary. Preserve the maintained Distilled_Water record and its rejected Demineralized alias, source-specific sterility, genuine W06 reuse and all original occurrence limits. No universal purity standard, process or sterility is inferred.\n\nThese conventions reconcile authentic new-owner origins; they do not merge maintained records, create source cases, approve every source association, or release roles/export rows. The complete original source claims and histories must survive native candidate composition and exact-byte independent review. No candidate has been applied.\n\nAuthor packet: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/central31-science-decisions-v1/`, handoff `cf18320110b4a4d1d3e065ff99495fbdc85dd5d9ef0c01f5cd3e9b87ebe4a015`, manifest `1b658aaab59eccdb355c37286af15ae114f4206fee94adc08aae12cbb2be82ca` (89 members). Independent packet: `preflight/central31-independent-v1/`, handoff `801675d2dc8878dc65726bc743bc5259dd54962dcbf60de03a4e3bf4df2e254b`, manifest `311b87ca77b933c86219a0efdf73517d72d68d5df65cb95f3311ae48e0fbe3fc` (38 members). Root rehashed both. The independent native review binds six targets/110 inputs; validation, source-currentness and rendering pass, with no new finding. This is a scoped scientific decision, not final candidate or release approval.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720120537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720201281","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720201281","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720201281,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkI4iQQ","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:10:57Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:10:57Z","body":"CENTRAL-24/25 representation follow-up: the shared named-stock scopes are scientifically supported, but `PARTIAL` is not the native value for an unstated complete ingredient list. Use `UNKNOWN` where the source merely names a preparation. Preserve the original author packet unchanged; its `decisions.json` common-publication condition recommending blanket `PARTIAL` is superseded by this qualification.\n\nThe same concrete field remains in frozen controls941 (`tris_hcl_0_2m_ph7_5_dsmz273`) and955 (`hepes_2m_ph7_jcm556_1200`): the cited recipes name those stocks and do not explicitly say additional constituents are omitted. Their boundary conclusions remain valid; their completeness metadata requires a scoped correction before application. Controls280/938 have more detailed preparation evidence and need individual reading, not a blanket enum replacement. Full named-input Wolfe/Hutner lists must not be downgraded solely because hydration, amount, or final species are uncertain. Preserve all source/physical/role/export holds; this adds no chemistry or gate rule.\n\nExact independent evidence: `preflight/central24-25-independent-v1/findings.json` and native review. No worker or maintained file was edited.\n\nIndependent review supports all ten bounded nominal conventions and preserves twelve comparison scopes. The source guidance and controls correction is recorded before the accountable source-worker fix. Native review binds56targets/587inputs; all56 original records pass closed schema. Evidence: `preflight/central24-25-independent-v1/HANDOFF.json` SHA256 `7a24f3cf7a8229028ec7091be34a99e78e0e13b67832a383e1cfc6767ce275dc`; manifest `90ad498a098dbe1d4b1a446be09242ceba6649b53b2136e0d6cb65ad6c30d363`, all50 members rehashed by coordinator. Ten guarded drafts are separately under final-candidate review; no maintained application or release has occurred.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720201281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720201502","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720201502","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720201502,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkI4jHg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:10:58Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:10:58Z","body":"CENTRAL-21 now has an independently supported practical partition. Preserve `Columbia_Blood_Agar_Base` / `UNMAPPED_0118`, its generic UNMAPPED scope and all authentic history. Author one genuine same-path dependent correction from maintained beforeimage `29ed63a00d3f4f7a1652beee549526d625eef231f29b40691bd128d2f7608324`: retain the two vendor alias texts and sources as nonresolving historical `REJECTED_LABEL` entries with truthful partition notes/history. Do not repurpose the entire mixed owner as a vendor product or fabricate a maintained preimage for a new destination.\n\nThe exact BD-Difco alias and three positively supported dry-base occurrences can be routed to the existing seven-input Difco nominal candidate. Generic providercompound2046 is not globally identified. Oxoid source300/921 support one nominal four-input candidate; source300 retains literal variable quantity and its CM0331 catalogue, while source921 states39g without a historical catalogue assertion. Four older CM331 occurrences specify1L prepared base before blood and remain preparation-identity holds; do not substitute dry-powder quantities. All original source membership and separate Columbia products remain.\n\nThe accountable worker must publish the authentic existing-owner dependency and bind its actual reviewed after hash to supported vendor successors. This is implementation of the existing BIO-F06/BIO-F07 finding, not a new blanket identity approval. No maintained application or role/export approval occurred.\n\nEvidence: `workers/w07/worktree/.temp/columbia-continuity-independent-v1/`, handoff `262baa33bb32dc864e4a5d3da6bef1dc9a58fc23f18696e3436b9c7d102a84d9`, manifest `9b4e4bdde13e226fecf3dc04fde7b65aa3b37afbbb82ed16b3720c7131ce6463`; coordinator rehashed all2358 members. Independent Columbia scientific and skeptical reviewers read the current owner, seven source rows and three vendor relationships. The report-only evidence-kind correction and predecessors remain preserved; native checks pass within the reported scope.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720201502/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720201812","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720201812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720201812,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkI4kVA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:11:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:11:00Z","body":"The bounded Mc continuity investigation supports a shared nominal Mc/JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 recipe, with an original McCas preparation protocol as a positive witness beyond matching numbers. Preserve literal source forms, units, added water and preparation profiles. Generic CultureBotHT Wolfe also has the same ten nominal amounts, so this does not establish Mc as an exclusive owner or authorize duplicate installation or a maintained-owner merge. A single explicit source-association disposition must be reviewed against both authentic existing owners.\n\nThe previously filed SCI-TENVIT-003 correction remains concrete: preserve Mc's D,L-calcium-pantothenate name and0.005g/L, withdraw the unsupported D-specific `CHEBI:31345` resolving reference unless an exact same-form child is verified. Publish an authentic dependent-origin proposal. The JCM/NBRC unspecified calcium/B12 names must not inherit Mc's D,L/per-litre or CB's cyanocobalamin/X100 specificity. Branded ATCC MD-VS retains its positive phosphate/product boundary. All TV001–004, JCM887/dose/form, role and export holds remain.\n\nThe packet retains all8cases,71CultureMech occurrences,84separateKG holds and6excludedcontexts;65nominal contexts is only an upper bound. No source case, origin, owner correction or approval was fabricated. W09's earlier CB authorship is disclosed and is not an independent approval of that precursor.\n\nEvidence: `workers/w09/worktree/.temp/tenvit-mc-continuity-decision-v1/`, handoff `55be71c0d3e12f780159cf62efb2b96f5cd37433fb2ad4cb794cafb25446b843`, manifest `4369c762e0fd0c14b6d240a79870f61dcc8f2ec313295341160a8b939755dffa`; coordinator rehashed all442 members. Two primary researchers and a separate skeptic completed their recorded scopes. Four exact payloads pass closed schema and the full2956-record partonomy context; those checks do not waive the scientific finding. The report decimal correction and predecessor are preserved.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720201812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720241863","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720241863","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720241863,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkI7Axw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:15:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:15:27Z","body":"Independent exact-candidate review confirms **NOMINAL-COMPONENT-001**, a bounded grounding omission in the ten private nominal-family drafts. The shared nominal scopes remain supported; no maintained record has been applied.\n\nFive explicitly named component references in four candidates remain `UNMAPPED` despite supported existing catalog identities:\n\n| Candidate / zero-based field | Literal material input | Supported reference |\n|---|---|---|\n| N05 `components[0]` | Sodium hydroxide in the named 1 N stock | `MIM_CATALOG`, `CHEBI:32145` (`Naoh.yaml`) |\n| N08 `components[2]` | NaCl, 10 g per source batch | `MIM_CATALOG`, `CHEBI:26710` (`Nacl.yaml`) |\n| N09 `components[3]` | NaCl, 1 g per source batch | `MIM_CATALOG`, `CHEBI:26710` (`Nacl.yaml`) |\n| N09 `components[0]` | Nitrilotriacetic acid, 1.5 g per source batch | `MIM_CATALOG`, `CHEBI:44557` (`Nitrilotriacetic_Acid.yaml`) |\n| N10 `components[0]` | Nitrilotriacetic acid, 10 g per source batch | `MIM_CATALOG`, `CHEBI:44557` (`Nitrilotriacetic_Acid.yaml`) |\n\nThe material names are explicit in the preserved DSMZ330/110/78/110a, JCM470/221/900/979, DSMZ792/590/1144 and ATCC1190/1191 primary recipe captures. The current primary ChEBI pages verify [sodium hydroxide](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:32145), [sodium chloride](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:26710) and [nitrilotriacetic acid](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:44557). The exact active catalog records and labels were checked. These references describe the named nominal material or recipe input; they do not exact-map the whole stock to a pure compound, specify dissolved species after titration, or assign a role.\n\nAdd the five references through the existing guarded private composition route, preserving exact quantities, unknown percentage/volume/handling details, all source profiles and ordered history. Also inspect the remaining explicitly form-supported inputs for similarly feasible grounding; this finding does not certify that every remaining `UNMAPPED` part is scientifically unresolved. Do not guess a hydrate, stereoisomer, buffer stoichiometry, diluted-acid formulation, nested-stock equality or an alternative pH reagent. In particular the Tris moiety, malformed Hutner molybdate, source-qualified Mn hydrate and alternative NaOH/H2SO4 entries retain their precise limitations.\n\nIndependent in-memory counterfactual checks with only these five reference additions pass the native closed schema and full catalog partonomy. The actual ten drafts, all original proposals and maintained corpus remain unchanged. All ten actual drafts also pass native closed schema/roundtrip/partonomy and diagnostic local registry projection. This is a source-grounding completion finding; it does not withdraw the supported ten nominal scopes or grant campaign application/export approval.\n\nExact evidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/family-nominal-candidates-independent-v1/finding-grounding-proof.json`, with candidate, catalog, recipe and primary-response hashes. The reviewed author handoff is `52fa8da3441405dca0b20ea950e2be724e4b568722e868f089944ea6ce73670a`; candidate index `f079276017c41efefdf98ad443033795ce170a408c8e49f50b80f96aab7d7630`. This draft was prepared before a correction; only the coordinator may publish it.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720241863/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720269879","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720269879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720269879,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkI8uNw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:18:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:18:32Z","body":"Additional scope for NOMINAL-COMPONENT-001 (issue 1237)\n\nThe required full scan of all 46 immediate component entries found 27 additional precise, source-supported child references left UNMAPPED. No candidate has been changed. Each entry is pinned to the original candidate, current catalog owner and primary recipe capture; official ChEBI pages were independently read. The existing five filed fixes are separate.\n\nN06: Glucose → CHEBI:17234\n\nN07: L-Cysteine·HCl·H2O → CHEBI:91248\n\nN08: MgSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:31795, FeSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:75836, CoCl2·6H2O → CHEBI:53503, CaCl2·2H2O → CHEBI:86158, ZnSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:32312, CuSO4·5H2O → CHEBI:31440, KAl(SO4)2·12H2O → CHEBI:86465, H3BO3 → CHEBI:33118, Na2MoO4·2H2O → CHEBI:75213, (NH4)2Ni(SO4)2·6H2O → CHEBI:86149, Na2WO4·2H2O → CHEBI:63939, Distilled water → CHEBI:15377\n\nN09: MgSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:31795, FeSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:75836, Co(NO3)2·6H2O → CHEBI:86214, ZnSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:32312, CuSO4·5H2O → CHEBI:31440, H3BO3 → CHEBI:33118, Na2MoO4·2H2O → CHEBI:75213, Distilled water → CHEBI:15377\n\nN10: MgSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:31795, CaCl2·2H2O → CHEBI:86158, FeSO4·7H2O → CHEBI:75836, Distilled water → CHEBI:15377, KOH → CHEBI:32035\n\nTwo source-form strings (L-Cysteine·HCl·H2O and CoCl2·6H2O) need the existing recognized catalog spelling in component_name for native referential validation; preserve the exact original literal in component.source and the untouched attributed source profile. No catalog alias edit is proposed. The nickel hexahydrate CURIE is held by two active catalog records; Section 6 says component reference scope is not a unique document key. This proposal does not merge or approve that duplicate family.\n\nKeep the 13 unresolved entries unchanged: HCl stock, Tris moiety, the two manganese-hydrate uncertainty entries, Na2SeO4 supplied-form lead pending a separate conclusion, diluted sulfuric acid, three already qualified bare/anhydrous comparisons in N09, KOH solution, malformed ammonium molybdate, nested Metals44 and alternative NaOH-or-H2SO4. N01 has no invented decomposition; ethanol already resolves and is unchanged. Preserve all quantities, source profiles, ordered histories and Hutner lineage.\n\nThe 32-link counterfactual (five filed plus 27 additional) passes native partonomy on a private in-memory overlay. This confirms shape only; final exact candidate review remains required. Recommend appending this bounded allowlist to the same filed finding before authoring any additional correction.\n\nThis is the composition author's extended finding, recorded before candidate edits; it does not count as a distinct independent review. The exact final32-reference candidate delta will return to the independent reviewer. Proof SHA256 `ffd6788e82fe3bd5f4a344f460cf7c9c6c56891cd4a25b0751163d088bc9a482`.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720269879/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720291988","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720291988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720291988,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkI-ElA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:20:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:20:59Z","body":"The independent whole-candidate review identified **COMBINED37-RCM-STALE-PART-NOTE-001**, a minor active-note inconsistency in TARGET-032, `Reinforced_Clostridial_Medium.yaml` (candidate SHA256c786cffe4421fc8d259f23ef43741071d6281d8cbe3ab4ce5389dabb08d82034). Its `components[0]` now correctly points to generic Peptone `mesh:D010461`, conditional on the actual external parent, but `component_assertion.notes` still says generic peptone remains UNMAPPED. The manufacturer formula and supported edge are unchanged; this is composition wording drift, not a new chemical identity finding.\n\nRecord this before the composition author's correction: append an immutable guarded successor that updates the active note to the actual bounded component resolution and preserves the original note/history, all quantities, complete-formula qualification, unresolved parts and real dependency block. Do not downgrade the supported edge to silence the note or fabricate a standalone partonomy pass. The exact changed payload must return for independent review.\n\nThis continues the existing COMBINED37 component-grounding scope. Independent evidence: `workers/w07/worktree/.temp/combined37-final-candidate-independent-v1/review/skeptical/finding-rcm-stale-note.json`; reviewer `/root/combined37_skeptic`. Primary captures and exact current/progenitor payload hashes are retained there. No maintained data has been applied.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720291988/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720346275","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720346275","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720346275,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJBYow","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:27:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:27:00Z","body":"The final independent ten-vitamin disposition is complete: document one common nominal recipe association linked to both authentic Mc and generic CB Wolfe source profiles, retain the existing records separately, and install neither proposed source-number owner. Report-local group TENVIT-NOMINAL-RECIPE-GROUP-001 is reconciliation metadata, not a new ingredient CURIE, exported node, synonym or exact identity predicate. No exclusive owner is chosen and no maintained records are merged.\n\nThe original McCas methods provide positive preparation evidence alongside the JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 tables and actual Mc/CB blocks. Preserve Mc G_PER_L/D,L-calcium/genericB12, CB MG_PER_L/cyanocobalamin and separate X100 metadata, and the JCM/NBRC batch masses plus1L added water and source-local preparation. Do not infer Mc or CB preparation from the independent protocol, final-volume concentration from added water, or source-specific child identity from a nominal comparison.\n\nC-P-JCM197 and vm1201-prop-nbrc903-vitamin remain authentic evidence proposals but are not selected for owner installation. Their original source-case links, quantities and histories are preserved. The genuine CB dependency and narrow Mc SCI-TENVIT-003 correction remain separate existing-owner work, with final exact-payload review required. Exact finished-stock equivalence and a unique JCM/NBRC-to-Mc/CB owner edge remain unestablished; zero new exact routes are approved. This does not prevent representing the supported nominal association now.\n\nAll8cases,71CultureMech occurrences,84KGholds and6exclusions remain;65contexts is only an upper bound. ATCC MD-VS's positive phosphate/product boundary, TV001–004 and all source/form/role/export holds remain. No new finding was identified.\n\nEvidence: workers/w04/worktree/.temp/tenvit-final-disposition-v1 under the campaign root; HANDOFF.md SHA2563e924e11c8f1ec20216a7f8f91a41b9963241213e47f4a2e2ba4e6533d2d7ba4; manifest1c15a87101e16bfceabd1107e790d4595e40f05e25ee615518bf6133073492a2, all282 members rehashed by coordinator. Separate scientific, skeptical and final assembly reviewers completed the exact disposition; the native pair binds6scopedtargets/131inputs and passes its unchanged native checks. This is a completed source-association decision, not unseen-candidate or release approval.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720346275/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720405936","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720405936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720405936,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJFBsA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:33:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:33:42Z","body":"Independent final-candidate finding C31-NTA-REF-001, filed before correction.\n\nW09’s independent science and skeptical review of the three composed CENTRAL31 candidates found ten explicitly specified dry ingredients left UNMAPPED in the NTA trace-element stock (candidate SHA256 `1c2038f0403fea83e225ee0a94d0f32fb23a4b1c87260860b3badbcae492842a`). This is a completeness defect for these source-supported inputs, not a requirement to guess every component.\n\nThe bounded correction is to add catalog references for NTA CHEBI:44557; ferric chloride hexahydrate CHEBI:86254; manganese dichloride tetrahydrate CHEBI:86368; cobalt dichloride hexahydrate CHEBI:53503; calcium chloride dihydrate CHEBI:86158; zinc dichloride CHEBI:49976; copper dichloride dihydrate CHEBI:86318; boric acid CHEBI:33118; sodium molybdate dihydrate CHEBI:75213; nickel dichloride hexahydrate CHEBI:53542. The primary recipes, ontology/form checks and current child-record bindings are preserved in the reviewer packet. Literal names, masses, units, source-specific preparation profiles, original evidence and histories must remain; add truthful grounding evidence/history.\n\nDistilled-water grade and unspecified KOH titrant remain unresolved. Do not infer post-titration species, common final volume or concentration, transfer receiving doses, clear the NBRC1308 exclusion or unrelated MediaDive38/40 holds, or approve roles/exports. VFA and deionized water passed within their recorded limits and should remain byte-identical in this correction.\n\nEvidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/w09/worktree/.temp/central31-final-candidate-independent-v1/`; HANDOFF SHA256 `d8a861d506a589a093df0c76617a598b56031b850c527ed96234e7e1ca21b390`, MANIFEST `93ccb5a9b75eb4071c1f03fd9692c24260f676d87a74021df52d11c774e2e7dd` (600 members independently rehashed by coordinator). Original finding `nta/findings.json`; concurrence `skeptic/file-ready-finding-concurrence.json`; ten exact child/source assessments in `nta/component-assessments.json`, `nta/ontology-query.json` and `nta/child-owner-bindings.json`.\n\nTracked here with the existing preparation-family composition work after reading the current issue and all16 comments; no duplicate instance of this finding was present there. Correct privately through guarded writers, preserve this failed candidate and review, then obtain separate complete-candidate re-review. No maintained application or release approval is granted.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720405936/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720423542","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720423542","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720423542,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJGGdg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:35:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:35:40Z","body":"Pre-write serialization clarification for C31-NTA-REF-001.\n\nThe native partonomy check of the ten independently supported references alone reports two REFERENCE_LABEL_MISMATCH errors: the literal formulas `CoCl2·6H2O` and `NiCl2·6H2O` are not active catalog labels/synonyms for CHEBI:53503 and CHEBI:53542. The exact source identities remain supported; no gate or child-owner change is needed.\n\nAuthorize the bounded representation correction within the filed finding: component index3 becomes `Cobalt chloride hexahydrate`; index9 becomes `Nickel (II) chloride hexahydrate`, the verified current catalog preferred terms. Preserve each exact original formula verbatim in that component’s source field, and preserve every original literal source profile, quantity, unit, note and history. The other eight names and the two unresolved components remain unchanged. Append truthful correction evidence/history; independent re-review must verify both full candidate and literal preservation.\n\nEvidence: `integration/central31-correction-v1/label-preflight.json` under the campaign task root, SHA256 `3aca065599e6923f1ea0936bdd015d20c2f6e8e355901dda5a5a02035314f60b`. The ten-ID-only failed counterfactual is preserved; the narrowly normalized counterfactual passes native full2956-record-context partonomy. No candidate had been written at this preflight. No scientific uncertainty, supplied form, role, owner-selection rule or threshold is changed.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720423542/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720444589","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720444589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720444589,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJHYrQ","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:38:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:38:03Z","body":"Scoped resolution of NOMINAL-COMPONENT-001 and its additional27-reference scan: the ten-candidate v2 correction has now received separate complete-candidate scientific and adversarial review. All32 added child references are supported within their recorded source/form scopes; six payloads changed and four stayed byte-identical. The13 genuinely unresolved component entries remain unresolved. This does not close the broader preparation-family issue or grant owner application, roles or export release.\n\nThe independent review rechecked all ten full payloads, all44 genuine origins, all inherited source/history limitations and the relevant primary ChEBI forms. It reproduced native schema/round-trip/partonomy and projection checks, with no new finding. Original failed/partial v1 evidence remains preserved. Two component display names use supported current labels with the raw source literals retained; no guessed hydration, common amount or post-reaction species was introduced.\n\nAuthor packet: `integration/family-nominal-composition-v2`, HANDOFF `11d0869bdbf51fd3fea47f33818abcbd5a0d8edb8697d59bd690449e789e25f1`, MANIFEST `096aea28a4dc26c44aeb8569e608348c0475de5f36b051e450f462f92892de51`. Independent packet: `preflight/family-nominal-candidates-independent-v2`, HANDOFF `b1f9ac9348ea2f3a1dc3da30399e51e40ab6163dc2f75d9cbe7613f69de597d2`, MANIFEST `aab9dffee670e627c0bfac91fd87310ad12407217e118260431de926cca692dd`. Coordinator separately rehashed the44 independent packet members. Native final review has10 targets and614 bound inputs; it is a bounded candidate review, not whole-campaign QC or final publication acceptance.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720444589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720520960","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720520960","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720520960,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJMDAA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:46:20Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:46:20Z","body":"Concrete native-plan finding/disposition: EBIOS redundant create origin must not be recast as an edit.\n\nThe complete kind/preimage check of1,021 current proposal origins across935 planned actions found one mixed-kind group, EBIOS. The supported single owner promotes authentic `data/ingredients/unmapped/EBIOS.yaml` (SHA256 `130f1d9a20d6e16b9a10939a7251242d290bc8b13eb2a140be697e7b86cf87a4`). W01 and W06 genuinely proposed edits to that same preimage. W02 `a2-proposal-nbrc1132-asahi-ebios-tablets` genuinely proposed a new owner with no preimage. The native operator correctly refuses consuming that new-owner origin as a third promotion origin.\n\nThe exact composed tablet-family candidate has passed a distinct complete scientific/skeptical review: candidate `a5b147248539b039caa788e4d208afdebd24c59b218082a1b5b06f266184f09a`; independent HANDOFF `76a4ba5d9cfcfa93c5150406daecc8b21d05cbd9838fbb50ebe626e65debfe5b`, MANIFEST `afa45f56ebe1b4eea86a8dde3597bd1f9f156b497ea1275c1a91a12158398b96`. The actual three source contexts, two CM occurrences and historical formulation/lot limits remain. This does not establish a second material just because a source-number proposal used a new path.\n\nBounded disposition before application: W02 will author and ordinarily publish an additive native `source_origin_retirement` statement for `w02::a2-proposal-nbrc1132-asahi-ebios-tablets`, complete original object SHA256 `47b497f7e9b2f764683bddb7479a891be28fa772716d84dd127238033fb34587`, with an empty successor map. This withdraws only the distinct new-owner creation; it does not claim a fabricated replacement source proposal. The entire W02 contribution, raw case and original payload `3275012aad49e7d7e353507d106a3a26c8b2313fad80e5e587ade3bec857bc3c` remain immutable and bound as reconciliation evidence in the existing-owner promotion. No duplicate owner, guessed preimage, invented edit, lost source case, changed gate or artificial scientific hold.\n\nEvidence: `integration/final-native-intake-v1/native-origin-kind-preimage-conflicts.json`, SHA256 `2b691533c6ee0f394af8cbcf70b785879ff09b43610e67fc837fdfa26c2f885b`. The real source author must publish the statement and source-case reconciliation; the coordinator will independently verify it and the closed crosswalk before native application. No statement or source publication is implied by this comment.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720520960/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720546829","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720546829","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720546829,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJNoDQ","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:49:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:49:09Z","body":"Final integration finding: two conditional vitamin-stock references outlive their no-install disposition.\n\nThe complete native partonomy probe finds JCM628_Top_Layer and JCM629_Top_Layer still point to `kgmicrobe.ingredient:nbrc903_vitamin_solution`. Both genuine W08 proposals (`vm1201-prop-jcm628-toplayer`, `vm1201-prop-jcm629-toplayer`) explicitly made that reference conditional on jointly installing the NBRC903 source-number owner. The final reviewed ten-vitamin decision instead retains a report-local nominal recipe group, keeps Mc/CB owners distinct, and installs neither source-number proposal. Thus the condition is unmet; no automatic Mc/CB substitution is justified.\n\nAffected exact original payloads: JCM628 `13fe1d4d83dc56b5b51be169db7c2e6cdf3beb361d3724b4e3137df6b3e10734`; JCM629 `96947f16567443e18cfc3d1c03a53dbed95d9d16aa374f9106fdf2a17c2dd7b6`. In each, the sixth component (zero-based index5) is literal `JCM 197 trace vitamins`,1 ML_PER_SOURCE_BATCH. Full before/after and original proposal/case bindings are captured in `integration/final-native-intake-v1/complete-boundary-and-component-details.json`, SHA256 `ebc7be2afbf6db639a4047a3ab4793a872bc0c3bc657139ff7b084c78b58c48d`; actual native overlay diagnostics SHA256 `587fded3ac062aedd615ef84992a900e6b471233570123d13b206fb28bef5ab8`.\n\nBefore correction: preserve both original proposals and exact source observations. Produce guarded composed successors that remove only this unfulfilled catalog reference, retain the literal JCM197 vitamin input and1mL amount as UNMAPPED, and explain the reviewed nominal association and remaining exact prepared-stock owner requirement with truthful evidence/history. Preserve every nested recipe literal, quantity/unit, preparation/pH/CO2 scope and other component reference/hold. No new owner, guessed exact association, bulk redirect, role approval or whole-stock omission. Obtain separate complete-candidate re-review and rerun actual full-context partonomy. This is a real broken dependency in the proposed final set, not missing source recipe knowledge.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720546829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720876122","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720876122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720876122,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJhuWg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T11:24:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:24:16Z","body":"# Parent grounding follow-up for existing #1237\n\n`W07-TOPLAYER-PARENT-001` — open; root files/deduplicates before correction.\n\nBoth exact top-layer candidates still contain `FALLBACK_REGISTRY` self-grounding. Positive NLM evidence supports Culture Media (`mesh:D003470`), and the closer verified recommendation is `MICRO:0001408`, **slightly acidic microbiological culture medium**, for each prescribed finished preparation at pH6.1–6.4. Publisher definition/axioms specify5.5–6.5. The pH target is explicit even though titrant identity and CO2 uptake are unresolved. This is no claim about permanent/post-growth pH.\n\nReproduce against these unchanged inputs:\n\n- inputs/author/candidates/JCM628_Top_Layer.yaml — SHA256 `1c4fb43f836330e603fd161cbdfac7c82d1097eefae274f6f9336178ffe7128d`. Inspect the whole `ontology_mapping` block and retained preparation notes.\n- inputs/author/candidates/JCM629_Top_Layer.yaml — SHA256 `2dde04411faad2ed57f7f158e561590e8d4e7deafa7bf01c004ff9dca5b21654`. Inspect the whole `ontology_mapping` block and retained preparation notes.\n\nRead actual JCM628 top-layer instructions; JCM629 explicitly inherits628 with its distinct carrier replacement. Read `inputs/nlm/{0,1,2}.body`, then `review/science/new-primary/micro-publisher-purl.owl` classes1408/1404/1301/67 and the full term comparison. The publisherOWL hash is `ef21dbfab755143a9c390ad274d4e1405f344f6a8dbfbd749de09af0b4b54910`. Exact sources, original acquisition times, access times and per-input recipes are bound in the science ledger and full candidate comparison.\n\nThe accountable author can add the supported parent and narrowly scoped evidence/history while retaining local IDs and all components, source routes and holds. Native quality `NARROW_MATCH` projects `skos:broadMatch`; keep each separate registry `exactMatch` sibling. No new component owner or shared-identity inference. A real corrected payload and its independent/native review are still required.\n\n`MICRO:0000070` is not selected: its text includes agarose but its formal expression specifies agar. No agar substitution follows. Generic microbial/OBI/NLM classes are supported broader alternatives. Salinity, defined-media and other alternative boundaries are explicit; no universal exact-term absence is claimed.\n\nAll source/stock/form/quantity/role/export/application limits remain. Prior W10 parent searches honestly recorded DNS failures; this new positive evidence does not convert them into a prior negative result or misconduct finding. Science and skeptic proposed IDs refer to this single follow-up, not separate issues. No correction or GitHub action was performed.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720876122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6721145825","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6721145825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6721145825,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkJyL4Q","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T11:53:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:53:11Z","body":"The two complete guarded top-layer successors have now passed distinct whole-candidate scientific, technical and skeptical review. `W07-TOPLAYER-PARENT-001` is resolved only for these exact proposed bytes; this does not close the broader issue or apply records.\n\n- JCM628: `601d8e0cd0699f407b58755a26da3362e0823cb1c011bce04e246523472abb76`.\n- JCM629: `65375652cc7b0ca4e6e9fa82430b68ceb8fa50699e0b923deb4f7e3ff1688305`.\n\nBoth retain distinct local identities and use MICRO:0001408 through NARROW_MATCH, giving a broadMatch parent and separate exact registry sibling. The evidence concerns source-prescribed finished pH6.1–6.4, not post-growth or permanent pH. Each retains all six components and three unresolved nested scopes, including the JCM197 vitamin input without the withdrawn NBRC903 owner. No guessed stock composition, parent identity substitution, role or supported-export approval. The two genuine proposals retain their single frozen name case and two occurrence bindings.\n\nIndependent native schema, guarded serialization, four-row projection, full selected-context partonomy and nine controls passed. Actual MES, bicarbonate and agarose applicability was checked with its existing limitations; this does not approve whole dependency owners or the adjacent MES-acid proposal. Original self-review keys remain distinct and preserved rather than silently closed.\n\nReview: `workers/w07/worktree/.temp/toplayer-parent-successor-independent-v1` under the campaign root; HANDOFF `32ad52bbc9695c4066d56efeb25de905266db049ff1390c7ce732d54c426469c`, manifest `8fb89a4bf99fa0af622d31f6d5e6b994174c6180979dc0e43b2e995387c91e3f`, native YAML `ffed62725746f5d327c54228bef5187bb0cf0793490f147aa830a8760cf632cf`. Coordinator rehashed all2,537 members. Complete campaign plan acceptance, guarded application and final mapping/role/export review remain pending.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6721145825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6724234025","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6724234025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6724234025,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkMurKQ","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T16:47:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T16:47:53Z","body":"Read-only triage of exact cdff9ef796b6c2ecf112218be61843fc1928f442ff4a7ddd89758ea116be8cb2 confirms two bounded selected-owner conditions.\n\n1. CHEM-COMP-002 remains open in BOTH exact selected new-owner payloads: JCM317 7d2da1da0d6d56cd8db3bdffbda87c94fdc2457caa693f9506684472bf0f22e2 and NBRC1020 d6a2c6de6bb04cc2c7ea3fc2c97dc1a0227151caa331af1baed4875dfbe8651f. The plan nevertheless selects both create operations. Their notes, component assertions, current decisions and final successor review expressly retain the merge/proved-distinct-coinstallation condition. JCM317 prints 4mg Na2SeO3 +4mg Na2WO4·2H2O +1L water; NBRC1020 prints the same masses with unqualified Na2WO4. Current primary capture hashes fc01b236c8584bdfd647d572cf2cea9e3aa8b22012222effefa0862ba232176e and 6b1d7b346a5f5de9dfd758198e56ef05ad43d8c68361e2ba72c9fbfae9876b7c preserve those facts. No later common-scope/difference disposition was found in the consulted selected lineage or the complete live issue history. A reviewed common nominal scope can retain unresolved forms; positive form/applicability evidence can instead establish distinction. NBRC824's denominator hold remains.\n\n2. W09's bicarbonate continuity finding is supported. NBRC1321/1257 mutual union remains valid, but selected new payload f7aca68cf65299a813290c8831a568126f3f18eb4ecf50dec60c8f178246a61a uses missing final-volume/prior-saturation detail in generic84g/L/J451 as a positive distinct-owner rationale. Primary NBRC captures471a2ea8c7daff318ea0b79a4b7508d5be43f5b823d728d957bdeef3c3ad6e4b /3ed45aeb1e2bbcb57b21ae44d4dbee9be2ba8c260b77df5642f198c7cc30ad06 specify8.4g NaHCO3 +100mL water, CO2 saturation and sealed autoclaving. J451 official frozen MediaDive API7e4712df36431b233a73fd33c2800fb361518bb369aeab7df227f254d2981c9a names84g/L NaHCO3, autoclaved underCO2, linked to the existing1764 owner. Missing detail proves neither equality nor distinctness. #1166 only resolved the two NBRC sources; CHEM-COMP-006 only addressed their pointer aliases. Preserve authentic generic-owner history and both source profiles while deciding a common nominal scope or positive distinction; do not arbitrarily merge or create by source number.\n\nThese findings concern source selection/installation conditions; no actual B generation was asserted. Source scientific-review bindings alone do not discharge conditions retained in the selected payloads. Any successor must retain original cases, occurrences, histories and genuine preimages and receive exact-byte review. No repair, source apply, process control, GitHub mutation or gate change was performed by the triage author.\n\nCoordinator disposition: the old source attempt was cancelled after 27 edits and is retained with its native failure/recovery record; it is not an accepted source endpoint. Defer the three new-owner operations for JCM317 Se/W, NBRC1020 Se/W and NBRC1321 CO2 bicarbonate stock in the corrected batch, retaining all four affected cases and original occurrence decisions. The separately supported generic84g/L non-name edit remains eligible; it is not selected as a forced merge target. No identity equivalence, hydration or final-volume decision is inferred.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6724234025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]